			"Message": "docs(Grove): Restructure README with expanded architecture docs\n\nOverhaul the Grove README from a concise component summary into a comprehensive\ndeveloper reference covering the full architecture, component inventory, and\nproject layout.\n\nAdd a security callout blockquote setting the motivation for Grove's sandboxing\nmodel. Introduce dedicated Key Features and Core Architecture Principles\nsections with formatted tables. Expand the Mermaid system diagram with new\nsubsystem subgraphs (API/, CommonAdapter, MistTransport, SpineActionClient)\nand a connection-paths reference table. Extend the Key Components table from\n11 to over 20 entries covering Lifecycle, VSCode API types, CommonAdapter,\nMist transport, Spine action dispatch, ConfigurationService, and shared\nCommon traits and error types. Replace the simplified project tree with a full\nSource/ directory listing. Restructure \"In the Land Project\" as a Grove-vs-\nCocoon comparison table. Convert the Security and Compatibility sections from\nprose to mechanism tables. Add the Mist link to Related Documentation. Apply\nem-quad spacing (&#x2001;) consistently across section headings and badge rows\nto align with project formatting conventions.\n\nThe README now serves as a self-contained onboarding document covering every\nmodule, transport path, and security layer.",
